# @DISPLAY_NAME@ (Android)

Generated by botlish-android @TOOL_VERSION@ (the tool `android` of the Botlish
package botlish_android) from:

* the Botlish application library `@LIBRARY@` (manifest SHA-256
  `@MANIFEST_SHA256@`, runtime ABI `@RUNTIME_ABI@`, built with the target
  support package `@SUPPORT_PACKAGE@` for android-aarch64, API @LIBRARY_API@);
* SDL @SDL_VERSION@ for Android arm64-v8a, from the package `@SDL3_PACKAGE@`
  @SDL3_VERSION@ (`libSDL3.so` SHA-256 `@SDL_SHA256@`, SDL's own Java classes
  `org.libsdl.app`).

Do not edit the generated files: generate the project again from the
library (`botlish tool ... android generate ... -replace`).

## Building

The Android SDK (`ANDROID_HOME`: platform @COMPILE_SDK@, CMake @CMAKE@) and the
Android NDK @NDK_REVISION@ (installed by the Android Gradle Plugin when absent),
and Java 17 or later:

    ./gradlew assembleRelease

writes `app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk` (arm64-v8a, minimum API
@MIN_SDK@, signed with the debug key: a test APK).

## How it runs

`@ACTIVITY@` is SDL's `SDLActivity`, naming its libraries: `libSDL3.so`, the
application library `lib@LIBRARY@.so` and the shim `libmain.so`. SDL starts its
thread "SDLThread" and calls `SDL_main` (src/main/cpp/main.c), which calls
`@LIBRARY@_main` -- the application's ordinary Botlish entry program, which
installs its own contexts, owns its loop and returns -- and reports the outcome
to Android's log (tag `botlish-android`). Nothing in this project knows what
the application does.
